<title>GERMANY: German HEW buys 30 mln c-shares in Sydkraft.</title>
<headline>German HEW buys 30 mln c-shares in Sydkraft.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electricity group Hamburgische Electricitaets-Werke AG (HEW) said on Monday that it had obtained 15.7 percent of the share capital in Swedish group Sydkraft AG, laying the groundwork for a possible cooperation.</p>
<p>In a mandatory bourse statement, HEW said it had purchased 30 million of Malmo-based group's C-shares. This translates into a 2.5 percent voting stake.</p>
<p>The group however did not elaborate on further plans or on how much it had paid for the stake.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
